**Motion findings:** motion instants — stem removal ≈1000–2000 ms · hand release ≈2000–2500 ms · press descent ≈3000–4000 ms (mid at F-3500) · reveal between 4000–4500 ms (the cutter's lift/flip is a stop-motion jump inside this interval; the slab is simply THERE at 4500) · gather ≈5000–6000 ms · bowl addition by 7000 ms. Holds — stem-on ≈0–1000 (CP0 is prior-episode; stem-on hold is CP1's state entering the window) · solo cushion ≈2500–3000 ms · slab on cutter ≈4500–5000 ms · final bowl state at 7000 ms. What changes between states: stem star present→absent (CP1→CP2) · hands present→absent (CP2→CP3) · grid absent→covering (CP3→CP4, the occlusion that carries the swap) · cushion→red-dice slab under the lifted cutter (CP4→F-4500) · slab on cutter→dice in hands→dice in bowl (CP5→CP7). The grid in CP4/F-4500 reads ≈7 columns × 6 rows of square cells with wooden side handles.
**Sub-beats:** SB-A stem-on presentation · SB-B stem removal (pins retained) · SB-C solo hold · SB-D grid descent + press (squash under occlusion) · SB-E occlusion hold (swap rides here) · SB-F lift + dice-slab reveal · SB-G slab hold · SB-H gather · SB-I bowl addition + final hold.

### 1.4 Variables (§1.3 extraction)
1. Subject — cushion centre/radius, fill + dark fill, seam colour + seam count, pin set (per-pin offset + colour index), stem star (point list, fill, scale).
2. Tool — grid columns/rows, cell size, frame/handle geometry + colours, press travel distance, squash factor at press bottom, occluder opacity max (the swap's cover at press bottom).
3. Output — cube columns/rows/layers (slab footprint), cube size, cube fill/edge, pip style (dice/plain), pip colour/radius, per-cube reveal stagger, seeded RNG seed for pip counts.
4. Bowl — bowl centre/radius, bowl + inner (green flesh) colours, prior-contents count (white cubes already in bowl), final cube slot arrangement (derived from cube index).
5. Labels — input label text, tool label text, output label text, label font sizes + family, label positions (derived from subject/grid/bowl centres).
6. Timing — stem-off start/duration, settle duration, press duration, press-hold duration, lift duration, slab-hold duration, gather duration, final hold; phase starts DERIVED sequentially (never independent keys — a timing swap cannot orphan a later phase).
7. Palette — board, board-dark, cushion, cushion-dark, seam, stem, pin colours, grid metal/dark, handle, cube, cube edge, pip, bowl, bowl-inner, prior-cube, ink/label colours.
8. Easing — per-phase easing names.

