### 2.2 Construction choice
**DOM/SVG single-stage scene (chosen):** one SVG; board rect; bowl group (fades in for the final act); cushion group (circle + seam lines + pin circles + stem star polygon) with press squash (scaleY about its base); grid group (cell lines + frame + handles + occluder rect) translating Y by press/lift progress; cube group (per-cube rect + pip circles when pipStyle="dice") revealed staggered after the swap instant, then translated to bowl slots during gather; three CONFIG label texts. All geometry from `stateAt(cfg,t)`, a pure function evaluable in node.
Rejected: Canvas 2D — loses per-element ink measurement the A6 fit leg needs. CSS keyframes — phase state not evaluable as a pure function (A11 receipts impossible). Photographic/generated imagery — approaches the specimen; the technique is the tool-forced identity change, carried by geometry.
**Named deferrals (lawful, priced):** (1) CP0 prior-episode bowl tail (source 39–40 s) — outside this technique; the allocation discards it (departure table §2.3). (2) Hands — not built; the actions (stem lift, press, gather) are performed by the objects' own motion, the fleet's diagram form for performed-action techniques (T218 precedent). (3) The source's separate bowl SHOT (CP7 is a cut to the bowl) is compressed onto the single stage: the bowl fades in at gather and the cubes travel to it — a named single-stage departure, printed on the comparison's face via the allocation note in build-record. (4) Spare background pincushions (top-right dressing) — omitted as set dressing, not technique.

